WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.570
I have no idea just how much Nergal paid as compensation

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.360
for all the damage we did in escaping from Earth,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.360
but we did escape while managing to wreak havoc on all parties involved.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:14.660
There was love, there was adrenaline and there was friendship,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.560
making things far too intense.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:20.610
But in any case, Yamada-san, thanks for all you've done.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:58.040
"Charmed" by Aqua Space

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.640
Gai! Gai!

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.660
Say something!

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.430
Say something to me, please!

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.650
GAI!

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.370
Gekigan Flare!

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.820
We did it, Joe!

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:29.500
Joe, what's wrong?!

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.500
Joe, snap out of it!

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.250
Joe!

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.940
I'm sorry, Nanako-san.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:36.210
Looks like I won't be able to take you to the beach...

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.110
JOE!

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:38.840
Looks like I won't be able to take you to the beach...

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:40.450
Akito...

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.160
Don't worry about it.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.740
But I think the only person that can help him now is his lover, me.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:48.970
Wonderful!

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.720
Man, just looking at these data sheets is getting me excited!

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.730
I hear that we're getting three more pilots.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.990
Who cares about that?

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:02.620
But these Zero-G combat frames,

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.290
they're going to be killer units!

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:04.830
Err...

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.940
About Akito...

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.670
I sure hope these new pilots turn out to be real bastards.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:12.920
Why?

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.580
It's better for them to be people that you can't stand.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.100
They might die in battle any day.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.100
"Mm hmm" what?

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.920
Captain's orders! Listen to what I have to say!

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.490
Captain, we're about to arrive at the space colony at L2,

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.710
Satsuki Midori 2.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.180
Please return to the bridge.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.190
I'm sorry, Nanako-san.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.100
Whoa, this place is wide open.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:35.800
Looks like I won't be able to take you to the beach...

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.770
So careless.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.210
Looks like I won't be able to take you to the beach...

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.650
Let's see, Yamada-san's belongings for Earth?

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.230
Thanks to the sacrifices of Joe Umitsubame,

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.150
Oh, this must be it.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.350
Thanks to the sacrifices of Joe Umitsubame,

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.460
General Masaka's onslaught was driven back.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.890
Sorry to bother you!

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.170
But now Gekiganger 3 is hurt and missing a pilot.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.200
JOE!

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:54.150
Will they be able to recover from this loss?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.040
The colony will come into view in one minute.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.640
Lower Distortion Field.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.420
Prepare for docking.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.880
This is the Mobile Battleship Nadesico.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.140
Satsuki Midori 2, come in.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.440
This is Satsuki Midori 2. Roger that.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.350
You have a nice voice to listen to!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.300
Beginning docking procedure.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.310
Are you ready?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.940
Okay, okay! Leave it to us!

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:16.980
What's happening?

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.930
Brace for shockwave from colony.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:27.200
Get me a damage report.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.910
Satsuki Midori 2 is on our bow.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.120
Continue the course.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.190
Field Generator Two in engineering has sustained moderate damage.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.580
I was just talking to him a few seconds ago.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.790
I was just chatting with him.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.990
Megumi-chani, keep your guard up, and look for survivors!

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:55.730
Yes!

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.140
I want that generator checked immediately.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.090
Continue to monitor the surrounding area.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.160
If we fall under attack now...

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.100
What the hell is this?

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.870
Oh, how thoughtful of them.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:24.800
They did some good work here, I see.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.230
Inform all hands to increase security measures onboard ship.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.430
Emergency, all hands hear this.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.680
Someone is believed to have infiltrated this vessel.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.680
All hands reconfirm broadcasting of identification codes.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.450
Damage control crew, continue repairs.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:37.260
All others, remain in their current positions.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.040
Damn that evil General Masaka!

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.540
Look at what he's done to my Gekiganger 3!

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.990
But now someone trustworthy and reliable is joining our team.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.810
His name is Ryuzaki Tetsuya.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:54.000
He's a new source of strength for Gekiganger V!

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.620
Detected craft approaching from our flank!

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.040
Four units confirmed.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.710
IS the field ready?

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:01.200
Hell no!

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.130
We will need another ten minutes on the generator!

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.800
Have it ready for me in five, please.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.310
Increasing magnification of incoming units.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.980
Gekigan Cyclone!

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.820
Ken, finish him off!

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.680
But Joe!

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.920
What about you?!

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:25.880
Don't worry about me.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:26.760
Do it!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.780
Gekigan Flare!

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:33.170
We did it, Joe!

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:34.550
Joe, what's wrong?!

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.490
Joe, snap out it!

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.200
JOE!

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.930
I'm sorry, Nanako-san.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:47.180
Looks like I won't be able to take you to the beach...

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.590
Joe, you promised!

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.890
Wretched Gekiganger! Damn them to hell!

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:08.270
Oh, I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:09.410
Are you all right?

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.450
I'll defeat you with my army of mecha next time!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.790
Thanks to the sacrifices of Umitsubame Joe,

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.660
General Masaka's onslaught was driven back.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:24.300
But now Gekiganger 3 is hurt and missing a pilot.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.160
JOE!

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.630
Will they be able to recover from this loss?
Joe is the best, isn't he?

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.800
Stand up! You must stand up, Gekiganger 3!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.160
I only recently found out about Gekiganger 3.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.410
For our future's sake!

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:34.500
I only recently found out about Gekiganger 3.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:38.170
After I saw it, I feel so moe-moe!

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:41.000
I even started thinking about doing a doujinshi,

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.980
and having it out for Cosmike, just like what I've done before.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:45.730
Well...

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.490
More importantly... Who are you?

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.820
What were you doing in my ceiling?

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.690
Ah, you are right.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.540
Oh jeepers, I'm such a klutz!

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:02.330
Come on now, I need you to put me down!

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:04.240
Like by asking me, "Who says 'jeepers' these days?"

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.200
Ready to fire.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:14.840
Fire...

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:15.440
Hold it!

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:16.810
That's...

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.430
Aestivalis's Zero-G Battle frame.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.350
If they're friendly, they ought to be emitting identification signals.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.140
Have they been taken over?

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:26.810
No. They've merely forgotten their identification signal code.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.230
How can you say that with such confidence?

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.860
There. Take a look!

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.630
A white cloth signal on the towing wires.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:41.100
Standard operating procedure for towing.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:42.740
But that's for when you're towing cars!

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:46.670
If only the Jovian Lizards were as fashionable as these people are.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:09.610
Man, that was a drag. Jeez.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.520
A woman?

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.640
Hey, where're the Bath?

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:16.950
Then I want food.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.630
Er.., well...

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.830
Could you tell me your name?

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.750
Before asking other's, you should tell yours.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.670
I'm Misumaru Yurika, captain of this vessel.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.550
Er.., Excuse me?

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.670
I'm Subaru Ryoko.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:35.970
So, where're the Bath?

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.480
Were there only four Zero-G frames left?

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.960
There's one back in what's left of the colony hangar.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.060
Four was all I could manage to bring at once.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.480
What about the two remaining pilots?

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.730
I have no idea. Could be alive, could be dead.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.210
I'm alive!

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.700
Hello, I'm Amano Hikaru, another pilot!

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.820
My blood type is B. I'm an Ophiuchus and I'm eighteen.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.930
Among my favorite foods are pizza crust edges,
and slightly soggy rice crackers.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:07.030
Nice to be working with you!

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.800
Was that not interesting enough?

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.160
Oh, no.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.670
Guess two out of three isn't bad.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.620
Don't kill me yet.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:23.800
Izumi-chan!

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:27.220
You're alive! Where are you now?

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:30.140
That I cannot say.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.870
In any case, try opening the tool box?

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.430
The fresh air is so good!

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.420
Damn you!

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:12.430
Oh no! Don't!

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.580
Please don't pack me in.

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.390
I'm not a mackerel that must be canned.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.800
That's the other pilot, Maki lzumi. You'll find out about her later.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.050
After the maintenance and re-arming of the Aestivalis are done.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:48.010
I want you to search for any remaining survivors, and bring back the remaining Aestivalis.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:49.350
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.400
Jeez, you work us like dogs, don't you?

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:56.480
Oh, when I came aboard, I broke in, so is everything all right?

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.840
I did do some minimal repairs to the hull on my own.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:01.940
Stand down from increased security status.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:05.360
What about these two pilots that you were already supposed to have here?

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.160
One pilot passed away very recently.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:10.130
This is the other one.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.280
You're kidding?!

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.230
This is not a joke!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.140
While I'm really a cook...

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.410
I knew it!

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:22.980
You just don't look like a pilot at all.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.440
That's right! I'm a cook!

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.310
I'm only a temporary pilot!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:33.630
But...

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.500
I...

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.900
Beginning docking procedure. Are you ready?

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.840
Okay, okay! Leave it to us!

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.450
What is it?!

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:14.760
No one cares even when people die.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:19.520
He's dead, and I'm the only one mourning over the loss.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:24.230
I care when people die.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:28.360
You're about the only person who thinks like that.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:29.580
Don't say that.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:34.400
Even if I decide to push myself as a pilot, no one will do anything for me.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:39.910
Doesn't anyone think about doing more on behalf of Gai?

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:42.570
I'm the only one struggling with this.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:43.970
I'm the only one tormented by this.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.910
I'm the only one who doesn't know what to do!

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:47.940
None of this makes sense anymore.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:01.960
You're not alone.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:06.510
I'm sorry.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:12.820
Everyone wants to be spoiled sometimes.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:15.740
I got it!

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.490
I've been hiding behind something.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:21.170
Yeah, that's got to be it.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:22.770
I've got to try harder!

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.090
I'm going to give everything I've got to piloting.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:28.260
Yes, give it all you've got!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.850
Come on! Move it, or you're going to get stomped on!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.840
Gravitational catapult, ready.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.600
Time to suck some more vacuum!

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.350
Leave it to us!

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.150
I'm counting on you!

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:44.850
Charging graviton waves.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.490
Subaru Aestivalis, launching!

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:56.800
Akito...

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:59.360
You should have launched along with them

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:02.110
after being encouraged by my words of support!

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:03.430
I'm so, so sorry!

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:07.010
But if you want someone to blame, you must point your anger toward the relentless fate that...

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.130
Looks like another one wants to go.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.550
Hey, you moron! You don't know how to operate a Zero-G type!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:16.080
It's not all that different from the land engagement type.

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:17.640
The basics are the same, right?

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:20.560
And you know those basics?

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.980
Well, I am a pilot!

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:26.600
All right, get the hell out the way! This idiot's going to push his luck!

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.660
Sensors shows no sign of life.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.080
I've found the spot.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:42.870
In a boiling pot!

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.530
Right then! Get ready to charge in.

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.250
We'll lose our energy feed from the Nadesico.

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:52.340
Energy Line

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.090
Out of Range

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:55.090
Backup Battery Remaining Time

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.010
Confirming backup battery activation.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:58.430
Start pearl diving!

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.270
In a boiling pot...

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.010
Hey, found myself a huge pearl!

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.710
Well, guess we'll start the salvage process.

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:22.790
Hey!

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:26.230
Let me help with something too!

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:30.490
Go for broke...

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:39.680
Damn it.

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:42.270
Emergency Sleep Activating

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.560
I'm out of energy.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:50.900
If there's a physical barrier between us and the Nadesico, then your energy source gets cut off.

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:54.030
That's the most basic of all the basics of doing this.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.210
Then, what do I do?

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.740
You do this!

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:08.040
Charging

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.550
All right!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.980
If you keep going, you'll smash into the Nadesico's Distortion Field.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.730
Oh, boy...

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:36.900
It's a Devil Aestivalis!

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:38.380
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:41.250
The computer's been taken over by the lizards!

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:59.760
You bastard, making us waste our energy!

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.010
Your total gross weight is much heavier than ours!

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.440
I'll close in on you with my advantage in speed.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.350
Time for close combat!

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:22.160
Oh no! It's too fast for us!

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:25.050
It moves with much more agility than you'd expect.

00:18:25.050 --> 00:18:26.640
What'll we do, Ryoko?!

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:29.270
I can never turn down a good fight.

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.500
I'll bust him up!

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:36.590
Here I go!

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:39.830
Oh my goodness...

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:43.520
Killer Move!

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.950
Double Attack!

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:49.490
Kidding!

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.600
Your body's wide open!

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.610
Damn, it's heading toward the Nadesico!

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:04.830
There's only the cook in that direction.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:06.860
Tenkawa, get that sucker!
...

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:08.120
I'm not the same person anymore!

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:08.250
...
Tenkawa, get that sucker!

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:08.900
Be careful about using a field attack.
...

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:10.580
I don't hide behind anything anymore!
Be careful about using a field attack.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:10.970
You risk damaging the Nadesico.
I don't hide behind anything anymore!

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:11.760
I'm Tenkawa Akito V!
You risk damaging the Nadesico.

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:12.710
I'm Tenkawa Akito V!

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:12.790
You don't do anything!
I'm Tenkawa Akito V!

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.500
You don't do anything!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.210
Here I go!

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.210
Here I go, Gai!

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:26.390
Gekigan Flare!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.050
He did it!

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:43.150
Oh, man!

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:45.590
Akito, you were cool!

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:46.370
Thank you!

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.060
Congratulations, Akito-san!

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:59.590
You did it! You gave it all you had!

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:00.960
Megumi-chan, thank you.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.890
Oh boy, what am I doing?

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:06.690
Megumi-chan...

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:10.220
Akito...

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:27.790
No...

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.710
A dream? Yeah, this must be a dream!

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.900
Just a really bad dream.

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:36.410
While it was a very convincing and realistic, that could only happen in a dream!

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.070
Right?

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.570
This is a dream, right?!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.990
Yurika runs, as fate forces her to.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:50.910
Akito anguishes, in search of a reason to fight.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:53.370
Jun cries, for he loves with all his heart.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:56.030
And Ruri whispers, "BAKA-bakka!"

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:58.460
As the Nadesico turns into a space-going Bastille,

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.410
the flames of revolution spread throughout the vessel.

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:03.660
Sudo Takeshi, of "God of War Goshogun",

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:06.400
brings robot anime into a new century in the next episode!

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.470
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.230
"Ruri-chan's Navigation Logs"

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:12.030
Let's watch it, everyone!
